==Trivia==
*''Baka'' (馬鹿) is a Japanese word meaning "stupid", "stupidity", or "idiot".
*Baka Cat Bros' name, outfits and hairstyles reference the [https://youtu.be/wf04tHHXZmE Baka Brothers] from the comedy variety show [[wikipedia:ja:ドリフ大爆笑|''Dorifu Daibakushō'']].
*In [[Version 8.8 Update|Version 8.8]], the Cat Bros were shown in the [[Cat Guide]] between [[Cat Kart R (Rare Cat)|Cat Kart R]] and [[Pumpcat (Rare Cat)|Pumpcat]], though they were removed from the Cat Guide in [[Version 8.9 Update|Version 8.9]].
**Despite still lacking an entry, their stage became available sometime after [[Version 11.10 Update|Version 11.10]], making them the second obtainable unit without an entry, the first being [[Evangelist Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Evangelist Cat]] outside of BCKR.
**In [[Version 12.0 Update|Version 12.0]], Cat Bros re-received their Cat Guide entry, also getting a slightly altered description, stating they join the fight from "The Battle Cats Unite!" instead of "The Battle Cats Together!"
*Unlike [[Cat Kart R (Rare Cat)|Cat Kart R]], they are actually available in the game they promote.
*Unlike their [[Cat Bros (Switch Special Cat)|Switch counterpart]], they target traitless enemies instead of red enemies.

